abstract: >-
  An evidence-driven Quality Engineering framework for evaluating
  Retrieval-Augmented Generation beyond final-answer accuracy. The work defines
  a Corpus-Retrieve-Rank-Context-Generate-Cite-Gate model spanning ingestion,
  chunking, dense and sparse retrieval, hybrid fusion, reranking, context
  precision and recall, groundedness, faithfulness, required-fact coverage,
  abstention, citation existence and support, freshness, authorization, prompt
  injection, failure localization, latency, token and cost evidence, repeated-run
  stability, baseline regression, observability and risk-based quality gates.
